* *nightowl.nu*
  This document contains a small whishlist of features along with a general
  sense of how to go about implementing them.

** Transitioning to JJ
   `Jujutsu` is a new-era version control system that claims to have improved
   upon previous models by selecting the most ideal features from past version
   control softwares (e.g. `git`) in a straightforward though probably
   opinionated manner.

   The impetus for this is to become more familiar with this style of working as
   I think it probably will make me better at keeping my documentations up to
   snuff.
*** (x) Create new local repository for nushell files
*** (x) Move files piecemeal over from previous repository
    ===

** Missing Implementations
   This section outlines the features that are in a state of partial
   implementation or that need to be finished in order to be used.
*** ( ) `genhelp` parse help files
    structured output that contains information about the usage of the command
    in question
*** ( ) `mmm` a model manager
    for working with, installing, and managing LLMs on the local machine.
*** ( ) `rsp` iykyk
*** ( ) `candy` dotcandyd dotfiles manager
    Finish the initial implementation of this until the final rust version is
    prepared
   ***
    ===

** Desired Feature
   This section outlines features that are desired but not yet implemented, e.g.
   more of a wishlist than thee previous section.

   ===

** Cleanup and Restructuring
   This section outlines necssary steps to clean up the code, the repository,
   and any assocciated documentation.
*** ( ) `kctl` a `keychain` extension for nushell that is not used.
    the reason for this is that the keychain and some associated tooling is
    better suited to be handled via a shell-agnostic initialization interface;
    this allows the same keychain parameters to be used
*** ( ) `ghb` download github binary release files
